 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Tokyo took a tea break.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 1.451,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "And left America with an unfunded bar tab.",
   "start": 1.776,
   "end": 4.737,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "The Fed hasn't moved, but your borrowing costs climbed anyway.",
   "start": 5.178,
   "end": 8.58,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Three men in blue ties blame the deficit, the Fed, or the vibes at Jackson Hole.",
   "start": 9.091,
   "end": 13.804,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "On YouTube, it's sixty-three stick figures.",
   "start": 14.245,
   "end": 16.8,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's what nobody on that panel is watching:",
   "start": 17.258,
   "end": 19.464,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "our biggest lender.",
   "start": 19.708,
   "end": 20.765,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "The Treasury's table shows Japan holds over a trillion dollars of our debt, and it's been selling since February.",
   "start": 21.09,
   "end": 26.988,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "I ran risk at JPMorgan; when your biggest customer walks, the auction sets your price.",
   "start": 27.498,
   "end": 32.653,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "The opponent isn't the Fed; it's a Japanese balance sheet.",
   "start": 33.147,
   "end": 36.409,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Two numbers show where the money went:",
   "start": 36.583,
   "end": 38.592,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "a Treasury page, and your phone.",
   "start": 39.051,
   "end": 41.083,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "By the end you'll read both numbers yourself.",
   "start": 41.576,
   "end": 44.398,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Since February, Japan has sold a hundred and twenty-two billion dollars of it, a tenth of the pile.",
   "start": 45.001,
   "end": 49.912,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "The Treasury prints the new total monthly, and that print is your first number.",
   "start": 50.295,
   "end": 54.092,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Tokyo has pledged ten trillion yen to chips, and if that works, it beats our bonds.",
   "start": 54.621,
   "end": 59.497,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "And here's what nobody says:",
   "start": 59.566,
   "end": 61.11,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "the money went home, and the tab stayed here.",
   "start": 61.354,
   "end": 63.781,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "So, the second number:",
   "start": 64.292,
   "end": 65.963,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "it's on your phone.",
   "start": 66.405,
   "end": 67.438,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Pull up Meta and find its price-to-earnings multiple:",
   "start": 67.821,
   "end": 70.782,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "that's the share of the price that's profit not yet earned, and a higher yield discounts it.",
   "start": 71.223,
   "end": 75.461,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "The Fed still hasn't moved.",
   "start": 75.792,
   "end": 77.325,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Tokyo is still on its tea break.",
   "start": 77.603,
   "end": 79.612,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "And that unfunded bar tab is still ours.",
   "start": 79.705,
   "end": 82.723,
   "part": 1
  }
 ],
